From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2000
From: Stuart Shelton <srcshelton@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: cix: allow Sky1 root ports to allocate I/O bridge windows

Sky1 firmware provides translated host I/O apertures for the PCIe
root buses but leaves the downstream root-port bridge I/O windows
disabled; endpoints with small legacy I/O BARs therefore fail
assignment even though the parent root bus has a valid I/O aperture.
Stuart's own motivation, paraphrased from the upstream commit: the
hardware still has standard bridge I/O base/limit registers, so
allowing the PCI core to size and program a downstream I/O window
fixes the assignment failures on real Sky1 endpoints.

Scope the fix to CIX Sky1 root ports (vendor 0x17cd, device 0x0100,
on the root bus) and only when the parent bus already exposes an
I/O resource, then mark the standard bridge I/O window as assignable
so normal PCI resource sizing/programming can handle the endpoint
BARs.  Do not broaden this into a generic bridge quirk -- the
exact-ID gate and the parent-I/O-aperture guard are what keep the
fallback from mis-firing on non-CIX hardware or on CIX hardware
whose firmware did publish a normal bridge window.

Ported from srcshelton/gentoo-ebuilds:
  40093-pci-cix-enable-root-port-io-window-assignment.patch

Signed-off-by: Stuart Shelton <srcshelton@gmail.com>
[ported: applied verbatim from srcshelton/gentoo-ebuilds
  40093-pci-cix-enable-root-port-io-window-assignment.patch]
Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/pci/probe.c b/drivers/pci/probe.c
index dd0abbc63..2435cbed6 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/probe.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/probe.c
@@ -417,6 +417,24 @@ static void pci_read_bridge_io(struct pci_dev *dev, struct resource *res,
 	}
 }
 
+static bool pci_bridge_has_parent_io_window(struct pci_dev *dev)
+{
+	struct resource *res;
+
+	pci_bus_for_each_resource(dev->bus, res) {
+		if (res && resource_type(res) == IORESOURCE_IO)
+			return true;
+	}
+
+	return false;
+}
+
+static bool pci_bridge_is_cix_sky1_root_port(struct pci_dev *dev)
+{
+	return pci_is_root_bus(dev->bus) &&
+	       dev->vendor == 0x17cd && dev->device == 0x0100;
+}
+
 static void pci_read_bridge_mmio(struct pci_dev *dev, struct resource *res,
 				 bool log)
 {
@@ -525,6 +543,21 @@ static void pci_read_bridge_windows(struct pci_dev *bridge)
 	if (io) {
 		bridge->io_window = 1;
 		pci_read_bridge_io(bridge, &res, true);
+	} else if (pci_bridge_is_cix_sky1_root_port(bridge) &&
+		   pci_bridge_has_parent_io_window(bridge)) {
+		/*
+		 * Sky1 firmware exposes a translated host I/O aperture for
+		 * each PCIe root bus, but leaves the root-port bridge I/O
+		 * window disabled. The hardware still has standard bridge I/O
+		 * base/limit registers, so allow resource assignment to size
+		 * and program a downstream I/O window for endpoints with small
+		 * legacy I/O BARs.
+		 */
+		bridge->io_window = 1;
+		bridge->io_window_1k = 0;
+		pci_info(bridge,
+			 "CIX Sky1 root port: enabling allocatable I/O window from host aperture\n");
+		pci_read_bridge_io(bridge, &res, true);
 	}
 
 	pci_read_bridge_mmio(bridge, &res, true);
